      "writtenOn": "2023-02-14T14:55:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think this is necessary and in fact it is probably dangerous as there are java libraries which are not direct dependencies of the apex, e.g. they are dependencies of a `bootclasspath_fragment`.\n\nIt is safer to just call `WalkPayloadDeps` instead.\n\nThe first thing you should do in the callback you pass to `WalkPayloadDeps` is something like this:\n```\nif !android.IsDepInSameApex(ctx, a, dep) {\n    return false\n}\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2995,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 2998,
        "endChar": 72
      },
      "revId": "004619d2cdbd95f87cf689991360c775dd6f2fff",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "46a1270e_0094224b",
        "filename": "apex/apex.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 3009,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-14T14:55:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I would not bother doing this. It might save some time but at the expense of correctness. Module names are not unique so you may accidentally ignore a module that you needed to check. Each module can have multiple variants and there is nothing stopping a module from depending on multiple variants of the same module. Also, Soong supports namespaces so it is possible for modules in different namespaces to have the same name.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3004,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 3009,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "004619d2cdbd95f87cf689991360c775dd6f2fff",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fbc6d237_3d5f9524",
        "filename": "apex/apex.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 3010,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-14T14:55:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This only checks for `java_sdk_library` but we also need to check for `java_library` as well as `java_import` and `java_sdk_library_import`.\n\nI would recommend that you use the `java.PermittedPackagesForUpdatableBootJars` interface instead. That will provide you with a list of permitted packages.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3010,
        "startChar": 25,
        "endLine": 3010,
        "endChar": 41
      },
      "revId": "004619d2cdbd95f87cf689991360c775dd6f2fff",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
